# @plurnk/plurnk-mimetypes — operator knobs (.env.defaults standard, #52).
# Ships in the tarball; the daemon assembles it into the boot floor
# set-if-unset. Empty value = unset.

# PLURNK_MIMETYPES_SEARCH_EXCLUDE — comma-separated project-file path patterns
# naming generated/noisy content that remains directly readable but contributes
# no graph, lexical, or vector search data. URI paths in other schemes are not
# repository layout and are not classified by this list.
# ProcessResult.searchExcluded carries the matched pattern. An
# entry without `/` matches the BASENAME; with `/` it matches the FULL PATH
# (directory drawers — hashed bundle names defeat basename rules). Glob syntax
# is the body-matcher dialect: `*` (crosses `/`), `?`, `[...]`; no wildcard =
# exact. THIS LIST IS THE
# CLASSIFICATION — tune it per deployment; there is no code fallback and no
# hidden heuristic (unset/empty = nothing suppressed). Sane default:
PLURNK_MIMETYPES_SEARCH_EXCLUDE=*.min.*,*.map,package-lock.json,npm-shrinkwrap.json,packages.lock.json,yarn.lock,pnpm-lock.yaml,bun.lockb,Cargo.lock,poetry.lock,uv.lock,Pipfile.lock,Gemfile.lock,composer.lock,go.sum,flake.lock,gradle.lockfile,*/dist/*,dist/*,*/build/*,build/*,*/.next/*,.next/*,*/node_modules/*,node_modules/*,*/vendor/*,vendor/*,*/coverage/*,coverage/*,*/.vuepress/*,.vuepress/*,*/.nuxt/*,.nuxt/*
